The built dist contains the whole .claude/ tree (5 agent files, 7 SKILL.md — one of them 565 lines — rules, settings.json) plus CLAUDE.md at 23 KB. Cause is Git::GatherDir running with include_dotfiles = 1 from the [Author::GETTY] bundle, so every tracked dotfile is gathered.

Git::Libgit2 0.007 behaves identically (there also .claude/, CLAUDE.md, TODO.md, .gitignore, .github/workflows/*), so this is a bundle-level decision rather than a per-dist accident — which is why this is one ticket and not one per repo.

Not a bug and it predates 0.006: the files are tracked, so gathering them is correct behaviour. The question is whether internal agent instructions belong in what CPAN mirrors and indexes forever. A consumer installing Git::Native gets the prompt library along with the code.

Options: leave as is (deliberate), or add a PruneFiles / exclude for .claude and CLAUDE.md in dist.ini. Decide once, apply to both dists.

